@startuml
' OWNER-MVP-2026-11-04 review: MVP core / cross-cutting. Core presentation/application/files or shared authority/recovery invariant remains applicable.
title Proposed release pipeline — artifact identity to runtime targets
skinparam backgroundColor white
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam defaultFontName Arial

rectangle "Exact source / dependency inputs" as SRC
rectangle "Authorized build / test / compatibility evaluation\nSafe facility and supported contract pending" as BUILD
artifact "Versioned release manifest + build outputs\nNo mutable latest tag as exact identity" as ART
rectangle "Separate promotion approval\nTarget/configuration/schema/recovery prerequisites" as APPROVE
node "Trusted target environment" {
 artifact "Web runtime artifact" as WEB
 artifact "Compatible worker / scheduler artifact" as W
 database "Owned schema/data\nGuarded migration, not overwritten release" as DB
}
SRC --> BUILD
BUILD --> ART : actual eligible output
ART --> APPROVE
APPROVE --> WEB : reviewed deployment intent
APPROVE --> W : compatible payload/runtime version
APPROVE --> DB : reviewed migration / backfill
legend bottom
 A code commit, build or workflow success is not target approval.
 Data migration and worker compatibility can require forward repair, not blind code rollback.
 No CI provider, runner, container registry, purchase or live deployment is selected here.
endlegend
@enduml
